# Typography (apply silently to every UI artifact)

Distilled from Matthew Butterick's *Practical Typography* (practicaltypography.com).
LLMs consistently get these wrong. **Apply automatically — don't ask, don't explain.**

## Characters — use the right ones

| Use | Right | Wrong |
|---|---|---|
| Quotes | `’` `‘` `“` `”` (curly) | `'` `"` (straight typewriter marks) |
| Apostrophe | `’` (= closing single quote, points down) | `'` |
| Em dash — sentence break | `—` (`&mdash;`) | `--`, `---` |
| En dash — ranges, joins | `–` (`&ndash;`) — e.g. `1–10`, `Sarbanes–Oxley` | hyphen `-`, slash `/` |
| Hyphen | `-` — compound words only (cost-effective) | en/em dash |
| Ellipsis | `…` (`&hellip;`) | three periods `...` |
| Multiplication | `×` (`&times;`) | `x` |
| Foot / inch — **exception, must be straight** | `′` `″` (or `'` / `"`) | curly |
| Trademark | `©` `™` `®` | `(c)` `(TM)` `(R)` |

Foreign names: keep the accents (François Truffaut, Plácido Domingo).

## JSX gotcha — Unicode escapes don't work in JSX text content

`<p>Don’t do this</p>` renders **literally** as `’`. Three correct options:

1. Paste the actual `’` character in source (preferred — UTF-8 in the file).
2. Wrap as JS expression: `<p>Don{'’'}t</p>`.
3. HTML entity `&rsquo;` — only in plain HTML, NOT JSX.

For bulk fixes via CLI, use raw UTF-8 bytes in `sed`, not escape sequences:
```bash
CURLY=$(printf '\xe2\x80\x99'); sed -i '' "s/don't/don${CURLY}t/g" file.tsx
```

## Spacing

- **Exactly one space** after every punctuation mark. Never two.
- `&nbsp;` before numeric refs (`§ 42`, `Fig. 3`), after `©`, after honorifics (`Dr. Smith`), between foot/inch values.
- Never hold spacebar. Never tabs for indentation in output.

## Formatting — pick one

- **Bold OR italic, never both.** Never bold whole paragraphs. Never quote marks for emphasis.
- **Never underline** in UI. Use bold/italic. Web links: `text-decoration-thickness: 1px; text-underline-offset: 2px`.
- **ALL CAPS** must be `letter-spacing: 0.05em–0.12em` (5–12%). Never on whole paragraphs.
- **Kerning always on**: `font-feature-settings: "kern" 1; text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;`.
- **Max 2 fonts.** Each gets a consistent role. No goofy/script/handwriting in professional work.

## Layout — the 4 baseline decisions for body text

1. **Font** — serif or sans (web is fine either way).
2. **Size** — web body 15–25px (12pt is a typewriter relic). Use tokenized sizes and breakpoint-specific steps; do not scale font size directly with viewport width.
3. **Line height** — 1.2–1.45. Default `single` (~1.17) is too tight; `double` is too loose.
4. **Line length** — **45–90 characters** per line. The #1 readability bug in responsive layouts. Use `max-width: 65ch` on text containers, not pixel widths.

## Tabular numbers

Numeric tables and dashboards: `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums lining-nums;` — keeps digits aligned.

## Don't
- No emoji or emoticons in formal UI copy.
- No exclamation points in clusters; budget one per long surface.
- No double carriage returns or extra `<br>`s for spacing — use real margins.
